-- two substances of the same provenance differing on a molecule: same source, same process, and one
-- covers what the other does not. The Commission's study records the cases — an anode copper
-- registered jointly despite different sources, secondary streams registered with primary ones — and
-- states that no widely applicable sameness criteria can be developed.
ProvenanceCollision : Type 1
ProvenanceCollision = (P : Substance) × (Q : Substance) × (sub-prov P ≡ sub-prov Q) × (M : Mol) × (sub-scope P M) × (sub-scope Q M → Empty)
